{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nThe compaction sweep's log, /var/gerrit/site/.rebar/logs/compact-worker.log inside the rebar-mcp container, is not on a volume. autodeploy.sh replaces the container on every src/rebar change (2-minute timer), so the log is discarded at each deploy. The Nov 1 PST sweep's log was lost this way, which left breezelike-travelsick-moray without per-phase production timings; Gerrit 3269 (f1fe7c6f587) added those timing lines, but they survive only until the next deploy.\n\n## Root cause\n- `_spawn_detached_sweep` (src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py:122-147) opens `StorePaths(tracker).log(\"logs/compact-worker.log\")` and hands it to the detached child as stderr. `StorePaths.log` (src/rebar/_store/paths.py:105) puts it in the `.rebar/` directory BESIDE the tracker, i.e. `/var/gerrit/site/.rebar/` for the deployed tracker `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`.\n- The mcp service mounts only `gerrit_mcp_tickets` (the tracker itself), `gerrit_mcp_code`, `/var/lib/rebar` and two secrets (infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:262-273; autodeploy.sh `mcp_run_new` mirrors them). `/var/gerrit/site/.rebar` is on the container's writable layer, so `docker rm` of the retired release deletes it.\n- Confirmed read-only over SSM on 2026-11-04 against the live container (`rebar-mcp-4496e9acd2a9-8092`): mounts are exactly those five; `/var/gerrit/site/.rebar` does not exist yet in the hour-old container; the container's PID 1 is `rebar-mcp` with fd 1/2 on Docker pipes; LogConfig is `journald tag=rebar-mcp`; `/var/log/journal` is persistent with an explicit `SystemMaxUse` cap (infra/scripts/journald-cap.sh), and `journalctl -t rebar-mcp` still returns lines from 2026-10-30, i.e. from earlier releases.\n\n## Approach\nFollow the existing precedent rather than add a volume: the MCP server's own log already survives every blue-green deploy because the mcp service logs to journald under one tag (docker-compose.yml:281-286, mirrored as `--log-driver journald --log-opt tag=rebar-mcp` in autodeploy.sh, guarded by `test_docker_run_matches_compose_mcp_logging`). The journal is already capped and retained by journald-cap.sh, so this needs no new volume and adds no new retention policy.\n\n1. Add a config key `compact.worker_log` to `CompactConfig` (src/rebar/_config_schema.py, beside `trigger`) with choices `file` (default, unchanged behaviour) and `stderr`, parsed with `_as_choice` in src/rebar/_config_sections.py's `compact` section like `compact.trigger`. It is settable through the canonical env override `REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG`, exactly as the deploy already sets `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH`. Marker: `# mechanism-ok: config_key compact.worker_log — 4f4d-9a7a-3b2d-4b13`.\n2. `maybe_compact` already reads `cfg = compose_config(repo_root).compact`; pass `cfg.worker_log` to `_spawn_detached_sweep`. With `stderr`, the child is handed the spawning process's own fd 2 instead of the file, and no log file is opened. In the container the spawner is the rebar-mcp server (MCP writes run in server threads, src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:110), whose fd 2 is the Docker pipe, so the sweep's records reach `journalctl -t rebar-mcp` with the `WARNING rebar._commands.compact: compaction fold timing: ...` prefix from `install_stderr_handler`.\n3. Set `REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG: \"stderr\"` in the compose mcp service and `-e REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG=stderr` in `mcp_run_new`; the existing compose/docker-run parity test then guards both.\n4. Docs: name the read command in docs/mcp-client-setup.md Troubleshooting; describe the key in docs/config.md and the worker-log sentence in docs/concurrency.md; regenerate docs/config-reference.md, docs/env-vars.md and tests/golden/config_surface.json with their generators.\n\n`file` stays the default: local and CI stderr is a terminal or a pipe a caller waits on for EOF, which a detached child must not hold open.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_config_schema.py, src/rebar/_config_sections.py — new `compact.worker_log` key.\n- src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py — choose the child's stderr from the key.\n- infra/compose/docker-compose.yml, infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh — set the key to `stderr` for the MCP container.\n- tests/unit/test_compact_trigger.py, tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py — tests.\n- docs/mcp-client-setup.md, docs/config.md, docs/concurrency.md, docs/config-reference.md, docs/env-vars.md, tests/golden/config_surface.json — docs and generated artifacts.\nOut of scope: shipping logs off the box (fab-dismal-haddock); the snapshot-GC worker's own log.\n\n## Testing\nFailing tests first, in the existing files, no autouse fixtures:\n- tests/unit/test_compact_trigger.py: with `worker_log=\"stderr\"`, the fake Popen receives stderr fd 2 and no `compact-worker.log` is created; with the default `file`, the child's stderr is the opened log file at `_trigger_log_path` (regression guard); `compact.worker_log = \"bogus\"` in config is rejected by the parser; `REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG=stderr` in the environment yields `compose_config(...).compact.worker_log == \"stderr\"`.\n- tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py: the compose mcp service sets `REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG` to `stderr`, and the docker run line carries `-e REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG=stderr` (the existing parity test also covers it).\n- Run the touched test files, `make lint` and `make typecheck` with the worktree .venv/bin first on PATH.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The compact-worker log persists across a blue-green MCP deploy (on a mounted volume or forwarded to the journal like rebar-mcp's own log), with a test or config check that guards the location. Verified by the tests above passing, and by the compose file and `mcp_run_new` both setting `REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG=stderr`.\n- [ ] docs/mcp-client-setup.md troubleshooting (or the MCP runbook) names where to read it: `journalctl -t rebar-mcp | grep rebar._commands.compact`.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] After the next deploy, the log from the previous container is still readable.\n  provenance: production-equivalent / live-call"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793790195801466001,"uuid":"955f3d12-80d8-41d0-b5c6-a5068032311d"}